From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:57:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep the exec_wineloader environment strings off the
 stack.

putenv keeps the pointer, and on macOS arm64 execve fails with EFAULT when an
environment string lies within ARG_MAX of the user VA ceiling (0x7ffffe000000),
which is where the first thread's kernel stack is allocated top-down. Every
new process spawned from a process's first thread failed with exit code 1
(wineboot: Couldn't start services.exe: error 731).
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index a6dc64c1..186501cc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -492,7 +492,9 @@ NTSTATUS exec_wineloader( char **argv, int socketfd, const struct pe_image_info
     WORD machine = pe_info->machine;
     ULONGLONG res_start = pe_info->base;
     ULONGLONG res_end = pe_info->base + pe_info->map_size;
-    char preloader_reserve[64], socket_env[64];
+    /* static: putenv keeps the pointer, and execve fails with EFAULT on strings within ARG_MAX
+     * of the user VA ceiling, where the first thread's kernel stack sits on macOS arm64 */
+    static char preloader_reserve[64], socket_env[64];
 
     if (pe_info->wine_fakedll) res_start = res_end = 0;
     if (pe_info->image_flags & IMAGE_FLAGS_ComPlusNativeReady)
